  "brief": "Marvell is acquiring Lumentum in an all-stock deal worth $115 billion, the largest AI-focused acquisition in history.\n\nMarvell / Lumentum (Announced): Marvell to Acquire Lumentum. Marvell Technology is acquiring Lumentum Holdings in a historic deal [1, 2, 4]. The deal is worth $115 billion and will be an all-stock transaction [1, 2, 6]. The acquisition is expected to draw attention due to its significant size and implications for the AI market [3, 7].\nOrganigram / Aurora Cannabis (Announced): Organigram to Acquire Aurora Cannabis. Organigram is acquiring Aurora Cannabis for CA$7.80 per Common Share [15, 16, 17]. Organigram has outbid Curaleaf with a C$561 million deal for Aurora Cannabis [16, 20]. Organigram will establish a global cannabis leader after the acquisition [18].\nFox / Roku (Pending approval): Fox and Roku Deal. Fox is acquiring Roku in a $22 billion deal [25, 26]. The deal is pending US antitrust approval [21, 22, 23]. The acquisition is expected to be cleared after a consent decree [23].\nFoodtastic / MTY Food (Announced): Foodtastic Makes Hostile Bid for MTY Food. Foodtastic is making a hostile bid for MTY Food [27, 28, 29]. MTY Food Group has replaced its CEO [28, 29]. No further information is available [27, 28, 29].\nRising Dragon Acquisition / HZJL (Terminated): Rising Dragon Acquisition Terminates HZJL Merger. Rising Dragon Acquisition and HZJL have terminated their merger agreement [30, 31]. The deal is no longer in progress [30, 31].\nBASF / Evonik (Announced): BASF and Evonik Deal. BASF is making a bid for Evonik [38, 39]. BASF's offer for Evonik has been rejected [33, 35, 36]. BASF has increased its offer for Evonik [38, 39]. BASF is still pursuing Evonik despite the rejections [34, 37].\nShell / XRG (Rumored): Shell and XRG Deal Rumors. Shell and XRG are in talks for a deal [40, 42]. ADNOC's XRG is in talks to buy a stake in Eni's Libya business [41, 42]. No new information on the Shell and XRG deal [40, 41].\nEdge Industrial Technologies / California blade sharpening company (Announced): Edge Industrial Technologies Acquires California Company. Edge Industrial Technologies has acquired a California blade sharpening company [43]. The deal was announced recently [43].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Government demands answers as Poundland owner rejects rescue offers for chain [44].\n- What’s Ahead for Private Equity: A More Selective Approach to Dealmaking [45].\n- 4 big questions about the DoorDash-Instacart deal [46].",
